 'Dubai to Egypt is a GOVS veterinary-entry and quarantine conversation, usually into Cairo, then UAE exit papers. Confirm whether an advance import permit or notification is required for your species and for a UAE origin, and which airport will inspect the consignment. Cairo International (CAI) is the working default. Borg El Arab (HBE) and Sharm el-Sheikh (SSH) are named cities, not automatic import stations. The usual building blocks are an ISO microchip, a current rabies vaccination, and an official health certificate inside a short window you confirm on the current circular. Only after those Egyptian dates exist do you request the MOCCAE export health certificate, commonly cited at 30 days from issue, and a live-animal product from DXB, DWC, or AUH. The 90-day MOCCAE import permit is for a pet entering the UAE. There is no Anaam, MoECC, MAFWR, or PAAFR platform on this arrival, and no causeway story. Follow the GOVS circular for any blood test it names.',
 difficulties:
 'Outbound Egypt files fail when HBE or SSH is treated as an automatic import station because the code appears on the list. A Sharm holiday ticket against a Cairo-named GOVS permission is a refusal at the wrong apron. The next miss is a MOCCAE import permit, which cannot export an animal. Quarantine length is the Africa-family uncertainty. Circulars change, inspection rooms close, and a crate that would have released the same day at a Gulf airport can sit in Cairo. We do not publish a day count or a quarantine fee. Certificate dates collide when the UAE export window opens before GOVS names a date and the Cairo cargo slot then slips. EgyptAir cabin-or-cargo on an inbound memory does not prove cabin from Dubai. Emirates and Etihad stay cargo on this list. A JLT booking to Sharm, against a Cairo permission, meets the crate at the wrong airport.',
 howItWorks:
 'Take a dog leaving JLT for a New Cairo compound, with the owner on EgyptAir the same night and inspection expected at CAI, as the timeline. About three months out, read the current GOVS import instruction, confirm whether an advance permit or notification is required from the UAE, and name Cairo International on that permission. About two months to one month out, once Egyptian dates exist, request the MOCCAE export health certificate so the window, commonly 30 days from issue, still covers departure from DXB, DWC, or AUH. In parallel, confirm the carrier. EgyptAir is cabin-or-cargo. Emirates is cargo. Etihad is cargo. Check the live rule before you pay. Refuse an HBE or SSH rewrite unless GOVS and the carrier confirm import handling. In the last week, check the crate for a longer sector than a Gulf hop, finish any parasite treatment GOVS or the airline requires, and brief collection at the Cairo inspection point.',
 airportsNarrative:
 'Egyptian arrival airports on this list are Cairo (CAI), Alexandria at Borg El Arab (HBE), and Sharm el-Sheikh (SSH). CAI is the working default for international pet inspection. HBE and SSH are named cities, not automatic import stations. The GOVS permission and the air waybill have to name the same airport. On the UAE side, Dubai International (DXB) is common for the passenger ticket even when the pet moves as cargo or in the hold. Al Maktoum, Dubai World Central (DWC), is the cargo departure on many SkyCargo-style consignments. Abu Dhabi (AUH) applies when the routing is Etihad. Confirm the live pet product toward the named Egyptian city. Write the same IATA code on the GOVS permission, the UAE export certificate, and the air waybill. New Cairo and Maadi collection should assume Cairo inspection unless GOVS names another port in writing.',
 airlinesNarrative:
 'Carriers named on the way out are EgyptAir (cabin-or-cargo), Emirates (cargo), and Etihad (cargo). Reconfirm each product for the UAE to Egypt city pair. An inbound Cairo acceptance does not transfer. EgyptAir cabin-or-cargo is not a cabin promise leaving DXB. Emirates stays cargo. Etihad stays cargo on this list. Any Abu Dhabi cabin wording is specific to the city pair and sits on /guides/etihad-pet-policy/. A wider comparison is in /guides/pet-flight-options-dubai/. A JLT passenger leaving the same night still needs a separate live-animal product toward the GOVS airport, usually CAI. A Sharm holiday ticket is not an inspection plan. Jazeera, Gulf Air, and Oman Air are not in this block. Confirm the live EgyptAir page for the UAE to CAI pair before you pay for a crate. Dubai Pet Relocation does not operate an airline. Tell us about your move after GOVS names the inspection airport.',
